:: Robin Console Visit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
You head down the hall and knock on Robin's door. <<He>> opens it soon after, smiling when <<he>> sees you standing there with your console.
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You adjust your grip on the console before looking back at <<him>>. "Um... I got a new game, and I've got a spare controller. Would you like to come play in my room?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"I got a new game on my console," you say. "Would you like to come play in my room? I've got a spare controller."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I got a new game on my console," you say. "If you want, we could play it together in my room. I've got a spare controller."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I've got a new game on my console," you say. "Would you like to come play it with me? I have a controller for you."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I've got a new game and a spare controller," you say, holding up the console. "Come play with me."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"I got a new game," you say, holding up the console. "Come on, you're playing it with me."
<<else>>
	"I got a new game on my console," you say, "and a spare controller. Want to come play in my room?"
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Really? Yes!" <<He>> ducks back into <<his>> room, then returns with <<his>> own controller tucked under one arm. <<He>> follows you to your room and drops onto your bed while you clear a space beside <<him>>.
<br><br>
You switch on the console and settle down with <<him>>, passing over the spare controller as the game loads.
<br><br>
<<set _rng to random(1, 3)>>
<<if _rng is 1>>
	You load a cooperative game and spend the first few rounds getting used to playing together. Whenever one of you makes a mistake, the other tries to fix it before the whole thing falls apart, and soon you're both laughing whenever a plan goes wrong. By the time you clear a difficult stage, Robin is leaning close beside you and already asking to play the next one.
	<<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<<elseif _rng is 2>>
	You pick something competitive, expecting a few easy matches while Robin learns the controls. Instead, <<he>> starts beating you almost immediately. Each win makes <<him>> sit a little straighter, and before long <<he>> is giggling every time your character falls behind. By the end of another loss, Robin is trying and failing to hide a smug smile.
	<<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gdom>>
<<else>>
	You pick something competitive, and Robin starts the first match looking confident, only to pout when you beat <<him>> twice in a row. You try not to laugh as <<he>> stares at the results screen, then <<he>> nudges your shoulder and demands another match, refusing to stop until <<he>> wins at least once.
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if Tamagotchi.isAlive()>>
	<<link [[Show Robin your virtual pet|Robin Console Visit Pet]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Play late into the evening (2:00)|Robin Console Visit Late]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Wind down (0:45)|Robin Console Visit End]]>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Visit Pet
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
You bring up the virtual pet and turn the console so Robin can see the screen. "This is <span class="blue"><<= _t.name>></span>," you say.
<br><br>
Robin shifts closer until <<his>> shoulder presses against yours, studying the little creature as it moves around the screen. "It's adorable! You have to look after it properly, you know." <<He>> takes the controller and shows you a few things you can do to keep it fed and happy, checking the menus with much more care than you expected.<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<br><br>
When <<he>> hands the controller back, <span class="green"><<= _t.name>> is already doing better after all the attention.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Back to the game|Robin Console Visit Late]]>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Visit Late
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>>
<<pass 120>>
You keep playing until sitting properly starts to feel like too much effort, then both of you stretch out across the bed with the controllers still in hand. Matches turn into conversation whenever one of you pauses the game, only for Robin to start another round once you have finished talking. Before long you stop checking the time, laughing at <<his>> jokes and arguing over small mistakes while the evening passes.<<stress -20>><<trauma -10>><<lstress>><<ltrauma>>
<br><br>
Eventually Robin yawns hard enough to stop in the middle of a sentence. <<He>> sits up, rubs <<his>> eyes, then starts winding the controller lead around <<his>> hand. "I should head back before Bailey notices," <<he>> says. "That was really fun. Let's do it again."
<br><br>
<<He>> gives you a tired smile before sliding off the bed, still looking pleased as <<he>> heads for the door.<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Visit End
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>>
<<pass 45>>
After a while, you both set the controllers aside. Robin stays where <<he>> is instead of leaving straight away, so you talk about the game, the orphanage, and whatever else comes to mind while the console sits beside you. Neither of you seems in a hurry to end the conversation.<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
Robin eventually picks up <<his>> controller and stands. "Thanks for inviting me," <<he>> says. "That was really fun. Let's do it again." <<He>> gives you a warm smile, then heads back to <<his>> own room.<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Alex Console Visit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "alex_cottage">><<effects>>
<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
You find Alex with your console in hand and bring up the virtual pet game.
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You show <<him>> the screen before asking, "Um... do you want to try looking after this with me?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"Would you like to play this with me?" you ask, showing <<him>> the virtual pet.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I thought we could look after this together, if you want," you say, holding the console out for <<him>> to see.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Would you like to try this with me?" you ask, showing <<him>> the virtual pet on the screen.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Come look at this," you say, holding the console towards <<him>>. "Want to try it with me?"
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Come on, humour me," you say, showing <<him>> the screen. "Help me look after this thing."
<<else>>
	"Want to play this with me?" you ask, showing <<him>> the virtual pet.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Alex.dom gte 15>>
	Alex stares at the little screen, then looks back at you. "You're joking." <<He>> points towards the farm. "I've got animals out there that'll die if they're not fed, fences that need mending, and you want me to <i>babysit a cartoon</i> with you?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> shakes <<his>> head and turns away before you can answer. "Grow up." <<He>> heads back to work, leaving you standing there with the console.<<npcincr Alex love -2>><<npcincr Alex dom 1>><<lllove>><<gdom>>
<<else>>
	Alex squints at the little screen and takes another look when the creature moves. "What... is that? A pretend animal?" <<He>> gestures towards the farm. "We've a whole farm of <i>real</i> animals that need looking after, and you're fussing over a fake one?"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> shakes <<his>> head and starts back towards the farm. Before getting back to work, <<he>> glances once more at the console in your hands and shakes <<his>> head again.<<npcincr Alex love -1>><<llove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Farm Bedroom]]>><<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Robin Console Gift
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
"Here," you say, holding out your own console. "I want you to have this one."
<br><br>
Robin's eyes go wide. <<He>> looks from the console to you without taking it. "What? No, I couldn't! It's <i>yours</i>."
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You keep the console held out, even as you look away from <<him>>. "I know. I still want you to have it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"Please take it," you say, pushing it gently towards <<his>> hands. "I really want you to have it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"I don't mind giving it to you," you say. "I'd rather you had it."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I'd really like you to keep it," you say, offering it again. "Please."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I'm serious," you say, placing the console into <<his>> hands. "It's yours."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Stop arguing and take it," you say, pressing the console into <<his>> hands. "It's yours."
<<else>>
	"Really," you say, pressing the console into <<his>> hands. "I want you to have it."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Robin looks down at the console now resting in <<his>> hands. <<His>> fingers close around it, then <<he>> pulls it against <<his>> chest before suddenly throwing <<his>> arms around you.
<br><br>
"Thank you. Thank you so much. I'll look after it, I promise." <<His>> voice catches, and <<he>> wipes <<his>> eyes against <<his>> sleeve when <<he>> finally lets you go. A few seconds later, <<he>> is already turning the console over in <<his>> hands and asking how to set it up.<<npcincr Robin love 15>><<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<npcincr Robin trauma -10>><<glove>><<ldom>><<lrtrauma>>
<<set $robinconsole to 1>>
<<if V.furniture.bedroom and V.furniture.bedroom.console>>
	<<run delete V.furniture.bedroom.console>>
<<elseif V.furniture.cottage and V.furniture.cottage.console>>
	<<run delete V.furniture.cottage.console>>
<</if>>
<<if not Furniture.get("console", "bedroom") and not Furniture.get("console", "cottage")>><<run Tamagotchi.bury()>><</if>>
<<unset $consoleAction, $trainType>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin's Room Entrance]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Robin Arcade
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You hesitate before asking, "Um... would you like to go to the game centre with me?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"Would you like to go to the game centre?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Would you like to go to the game centre?" you ask. "We can play whatever you want."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Would you like to come to the game centre with me?" you ask.
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Come on, let's go to the game centre," you say.
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Let's hit the arcade," you say.
<<else>>
	"Want to go to the game centre?" you ask.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour lt 12 and (Time.schoolDay or Time.isWeekEnd())>>
	<<effects>>
	Robin starts to smile, but a glance at the clock makes <<him>> stop. "I can't," <<he>> says. "I need to get ready soon. I can go in the evening."
	<br><br>
	<<robinoptions>>
<<else>>
	<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "town">><<effects>>
	<<set $daily.robin.arcade to 1>><<money -1000 "robin">><<pass 30>>
	Robin grins. "The arcade? I love that place!" <<He>> gets to <<his>> feet at once and starts getting ready to leave.
	<br><br>
	<<if $robinromance is 1>>
		You walk hand in hand to Starfish Street. Before you reach the arcade, you can already hear the music and electronic noises from the games inside.
	<<else>>
		You walk together to Starfish Street. Before you reach the arcade, you can already hear the music and electronic noises from the games inside.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Inside, rows of racing games, shooters, and prize machines fill the room. Robin slows down as <<he>> looks from one cabinet to the next, trying to decide where to start. "What should we play first?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[A racing cabinet|Robin Arcade Play]]>><<set $phase to 0>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[A co-op shooter|Robin Arcade Play]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[The prize machines|Robin Arcade Play]]>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Robin Arcade Play
<<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<pass 45>>
<<switch $phase>>
	<<case 0>>
		You squeeze into the twin racing seats and put a coin into the machine. Robin grips the wheel with both hands as the countdown starts, leaning into every turn as though <<he>> is actually behind the wheel. <<He>> clips barrier after barrier, laughing each time the cabinet shakes beneath <<him>>, but somehow stays close enough to overtake you near the end. When <<he>> crosses the finish line first, <<he>> turns towards you with a delighted grin before immediately asking for another race.<<stress -12>><<lstress>>
		<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
	<<case 1>>
		You take the two light guns from their holders and stand beside Robin as the first wave of enemies fills the screen. At first you both keep shooting at the same targets, but after a few rounds you start covering opposite sides of the screen, reloading while the other keeps shooting. Robin turns out to be a surprisingly good shot, and when you clear the final stage together, <<he>> raises <<his>> gun in celebration before remembering it is still attached to the cabinet.<<stress -12>><<lstress>>
		<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
	<<default>>
		You move over to the prize machines, trying the claw machine first before spending the rest of your coins on the coin-pusher. Robin leans close to the glass whenever the claw closes around something, groaning when the prize slips free. After several attempts, a plush finally drops into the chute. <<He>> bends down to grab it, then straightens with the toy held above <<his>> head as <<he>> cheers loudly enough to make a few people turn around.<<stress -12>><<lstress>>
		<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
<</switch>>
<<unset $phase>>
<br><br>
<<set _hasConsole to (Furniture.get('console', 'bedroom') or Furniture.get('console', 'cottage'))>>
<<if _hasConsole and random(1, 100) lte Tamagotchi.boosterChancePct()>>
	<<set _boost to Tamagotchi.rollBooster()>>
	As you start towards the exit, Robin notices a gachapon machine near the door and checks <<his>> pockets. <<He>> feeds in the last of <<his>> coins, turns the handle, then catches the capsule when it drops into the tray.
	<br><br>
	"Look!" <<He>> holds it up for you to see. "It's a booster pack for that virtual pet!"
	<br><br>
	<<He>> presses it into your hands, and the two of you open it together before leaving the arcade.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">Robin gave you <<= _boost.label>> <<= _boost.detail>>!</span><<ltrauma>><<trauma -3>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<if $robinromance is 1>>
	After using the last of your coins, you leave the arcade hand in hand and start back towards the orphanage, still talking about the games you played.
<<else>>
	After using the last of your coins, you leave the arcade together and start back towards the orphanage, still talking about the games you played.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Options]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Console Rescue
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set _resc to Tamagotchi.claimRobinRescue()>>
<<set _t to Tamagotchi.status()>>
Robin freezes when <<he>> sees you, then scrambles to <<his>> feet and hurries across the room, throwing <<his>> arms around you before you have time to say anything.
<br><br>
"You're back! I knew it. I just knew you'd come home." <<He>> holds you tightly, then loosens <<his>> arms and looks at your face without fully letting go. "I kept telling myself you'd turn up sooner or later... so I looked after <span class="blue"><<= _t.name>></span> while you were gone. I fed it, kept it clean, all of it."
<br><br>
<<if _resc.keyGained>>
	Robin remembers something and reaches into <<his>> pocket. "Oh! And <<= _t.name>> found this while you were gone." <<He>> presses a small key into your hand, smiling as you examine it.
	<br><br>
	<span class="gold">Robin gives you a dungeon key! You now hold <<= _resc.keys>>.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<speechresolve>>
<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
	You look down at what <<he>> gave you, then back at <<him>>. "Thank you... for looking after everything."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
	"Thank you, Robin," you say. "I'm glad you looked after <<= _t.name>> for me."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	"Thank you," you say, letting <<him>> keep hold of you. "You took really good care of <<= _t.name>>."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Thank you for taking care of <<= _t.name>> while I was gone," you say. "I really appreciate it."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I knew I could trust you with <<= _t.name>>," you say. "Thanks, Robin."
<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
	"Knew I could count on you," you say, giving <<him>> a squeeze. "Thanks, Robin."
<<else>>
	"Thanks, Robin," you say. "You did a good job looking after <<= _t.name>>."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Robin smiles and hugs you again, resting against you for a while before <<he>> finally lets go.<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>><<trauma -6>><<stress -10>><<ltrauma>><<llstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bedroom]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
